<article class="env-corollary" id="04W6">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04W6">Corollary <span data-tag="04W6">5.5.3.17</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a fully faithful functor of $\infty $-categories. Then $F$ is a monomorphism in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_0 \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be the essential image of $F$. By virtue of Corollary <a data-tag="06T6" href="/tag/06T6">5.5.3.16</a>, it will suffice to show that $F$ induces an equivalence from $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ to $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_0$, which is a reformulation of the requirement that $F$ is fully faithful (Corollary <a data-tag="01K0" href="/tag/01K0">4.8.4.4</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
